== 0. Preamble ==

Ensia is a compiler toolchain that operates on LLVM IR. When Ensia
processes a user program, it may inject, link, or otherwise combine certain
Ensia-provided code, runtime components, or transformation blocks (for
example, the AntiHook implementation) with that program at the LLVM IR
level. This Exception is intended to make clear that such combination does
NOT cause the user's program, nor the output produced by Ensia, to be
subject to the GNU Affero General Public License (AGPL) version 3, under
the conditions set out below.

